  "document_title": "Low Power Double Data Rate 5 (LPDDR5) SDRAM Standard",
  "document_number": "JESD209-5",
  "version": "JESD209-5 (original), with addenda JESD209-5B (LPDDR5/5X) and JESD209-5X (LPDDR5X)",
  "revised_date": "Published 19 February 2019 (JESD209-5); JESD209-5B (LPDDR5/5X) published 28 July 2021",
  "manufacturer": "JEDEC Solid State Technology Association (multi-vendor consortium standard)",
  "publisher": "JEDEC Solid State Technology Association, 3103 North 10th Street, Suite 240 South, Arlington, VA 22201-2107",
  "copyright": "Copyright JEDEC Solid State Technology Association 2019",
  "abstract": "LPDDR5 (Low Power Double Data Rate 5) SDRAM is a high-speed, low-power mobile DRAM standardized by JEDEC as JESD209-5. It uses a new clocking architecture: a quarter-speed master clock (CK) for command/address plus a full-speed Write Clock (WCK) and Read Strobe (RDQS) that are enabled only when needed, reaching up to 6400 Mbit/s per pin. The device has 16 banks in four DDR4-style bank groups; prefetch remains 16n. LPDDR5 narrows the command/address (CA) bus to 7 bits at double data rate, reduces VDDQ to 0.5 V, and adds link ECC, DVFS, deep sleep, Data-Copy / Write-X, and CKE-less low-power entry (a CA command bounded by CS).",
